    "slot_value": "Use campaign history to review trends or comments, and preserve past campaigns, published posts, and comments or replies if they matter for reference so the team can pick up work without losing context; also keep a clear history of what was posted, approved, changed, and when it went live. Access should remain limited day to day to the brands or campaigns each person is assigned to, and users should not change historical records. Retention should mostly follow the client’s contract and any legal or compliance rules, since some customers will want a longer history for reporting and others won’t. Audit record access should be restricted to the same roles that can see the related brand or campaign, with admins or compliance users only if explicitly needed for oversight. If content is private, unauthorized, or otherwise sensitive, it should be masked or limited as much as possible while still keeping enough detail for the audit trail. If a message is tied to a consent restriction, legal hold, or regional limitation, it should be masked or hidden from unauthorized users and still logged for audit purposes.",
